# Pixel Agents manual web (REST) provider requests
#
# Usage:
# 1. Start Pixel Agents: `npx pixel-agents --port 3100` (or open the VS Code panel --
#    the HTTP server always starts regardless of the "hooks enabled" setting).
# 2. Copy `port` and `token` from `~/.pixel-agents/server.json` into the variables below.
# 3. Set `cwd` to a workspace folder Pixel Agents knows about, or enable "Watch All
#    Sessions" -- see docs/web-provider-plan.md, Phase 3 ("Tracking gate").
# 4. Run the requests in order with a REST client that supports `.http` files.
#
# Notes:
# - Unlike the Claude provider (server/manual-hook-events.http), there is nothing to
#   install: `POST /api/hooks/web` *is* the hook. `installHooks`/`areHooksInstalled`
#   are no-ops for this provider.
# - `sessionStart` only stages a pending external session. A follow-up event such as
#   `toolStart`, `turnEnd`, or `permissionRequest` is what actually creates the agent.
# - Tool names are free-form -- this provider has no fixed vocabulary. Reusing one of
#   Claude's own tool names (e.g. "Read", "Grep") makes the character use the
#   "reading" animation, since clientMessageHandler unions tool capabilities across
#   every registered provider.
# - See docs/web-provider-plan.md, Phase 2a for the full wire-format table.

@host = 127.0.0.1
@port = 3100
@token = paste-token-from-~/.pixel-agents/server.json
@sessionId = manual-web-session-1

###
# Health check
GET http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/health

###
# Stage a new external session (no overlay yet -- pending confirmation)
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "sessionStart",
  "cwd": "/absolute/path/to/your/workspace"
}

###
# Confirm the pending session: agent spawns, character starts "typing"
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "toolStart",
  "tool_id": "t1",
  "tool_name": "Build",
  "input": { "target": "release" },
  "status": "Building release artifact"
}

###
# Show the permission bubble
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "permissionRequest"
}

###
# Spawn a sub-agent character next to the parent
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "subagentStart",
  "parent_tool_id": "t1",
  "tool_id": "t2",
  "tool_name": "Lint worker"
}

###
# Despawn the sub-agent character
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "subagentEnd",
  "parent_tool_id": "t1",
  "tool_id": "t2"
}

###
# Tool finished
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "toolEnd",
  "tool_id": "t1"
}

###
# Mark the agent waiting (turn finished)
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "turnEnd",
  "awaiting_input": false
}

###
# Despawn the agent
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/api/hooks/web
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "session_id": "{{sessionId}}",
  "hook_event_name": "sessionEnd",
  "reason": "exit"
}
